@781 = ~Killer Weapon~
@782 = ~Killer Weapon (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round / level
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

This spell gives the warlord's weapon a 5% + 1% per 2 caster levels (maximum 15%) chance of delivering a vorpal blow. The nature of the weapon determines the killing strike: a slashing weapon cleanly severs the neck, while a crushing weapon violently tears off the head. A successful saving throw at -4 prevents the fatal effect.
Some creatures, such as golems and undead, can survive the loss of their head, while others, such as aberrations and oozes, have no such vital organs.~
@7821 = ~Killer Weapon (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

This spell gives the warlord's weapon a 15% chance of delivering a vorpal blow. The nature of the weapon determines the killing strike: a slashing weapon cleanly severs the neck, while a crushing weapon violently tears off the head. A successful saving throw at -4 prevents the fatal effect.
Some creatures, such as golems and undead, can survive the loss of their head, while others, such as aberrations and oozes, have no such vital organs.~
@7822 = ~Killer Weapon (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 8
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell gives the recipient's weapon a 15% chance of delivering a vorpal blow. The nature of the weapon determines the killing strike: a slashing weapon cleanly severs the neck, a crushing weapon violently tears off the head, and a piercing weapon strikes the heart or brain. A successful saving throw at -4 prevents the fatal effect.
Some creatures, such as golems and undead, can survive the loss of their head, while others, such as aberrations and oozes, have no such vital organs.~
@78221 = ~Killer Weapon (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 8
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell gives the recipient's weapon a 15% chance of delivering a vorpal blow. The nature of the weapon determines the killing strike: a slashing weapon cleanly severs the neck, a crushing weapon violently tears off the head, and a piercing weapon strikes the heart or brain. A successful saving throw at -4 prevents the fatal effect.
Some creatures, such as golems and undead, can survive the loss of their head, while others, such as aberrations and oozes, have no such vital organs.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
Their hits are vorpal in 10% of cases, with a saving throw at -3 to avoid, for 13 rounds.~
@78239 = ~Vorpal Blow!~

@783 = ~Elemental Shock~
@784 = ~Elemental Shock (Evocation)
Level: 8
Range: 40m
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 1 round
Area of Effect: 9-meter radius
Saving Throw: special

The warlord created this spell after realizing how destructive a sudden change in temperature can be. To apply this principle to potential victims, this spell simply allows the caster to cast simultaneously two offensive spells of opposite nature: once casting is done, the mage extends both palms toward the target, and a fireball shoots from his left hand and a frost orb from his right. The damage is 10D6 for fireball and 10D4 +10 for the frost orb (save vs. spell to halve).
But the frost orb reaches the target more slowly than the fireball, so the victims are first burnt then frozen afterwards. They thus suffer a metabolic shock that doubles the damage they receive if they fail a save vs. polymorph at -2.
Stone Golems are particularly susceptible to this spell, for which the saving throw is reduced by -4.
The spell has a special effect against creatures immune to fire or cold: those who fail a saving throw vs. polymorph suffer normal damage (not doubled) of the element they are immune to, the opposing element enables the spell to overcome that immunity.~
@7841 = ~Elemental Shock (Evocation)
Level: 8
Range: 40m
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 9-meter radius
Saving Throw: special

The warlord created this spell after realizing how destructive a sudden change in temperature can be. To apply this principle to potential victims, this spell simply allows the caster to cast simultaneously two offensive spells of opposite nature: once casting is done, the mage extends both palms toward the target, and a fireball shoots from his left hand and a frost orb from his right. The damage is 10D6 for fireball and 10D4 +10 for the frost orb (save vs. spell to halve).
But the frost orb reaches the target more slowly than the fireball, so the victims are first burnt then frozen afterwards. They thus suffer a metabolic shock that doubles the damage they receive if they fail a saving throw vs. polymorph at -2.
Stone Golems are particularly susceptible to this spell, for which the saving throw is reduced by -4.
The spell has a special effect against creatures immune to fire or cold: those who fail a saving throw vs. polymorph suffer normal damage (not doubled) of the element they are immune to, the opposing element enables the spell to overcome that immunity.~

@785 = ~Mirror Double~
@786 = ~Mirror Double (Illusion)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round / level
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows the warlord to create a mirror double that can imitate his actions. More powerful than the 6th-level Physical Image spell, Mirror Double is created from the reflection of the caster and thus is no longer directly linked to him. So it can move independently of the caster and engage in combat. It cannot perform other actions such as opening a door or holding a conversation. Its illusory nature does not allow it to fully interact with the physical world.
When fighting, it can affect all creatures who believe it is real (and therefore cannot affect a creature immune to illusions). In this case, it fights with 60% of the warlord's abilities (THAC0, saving throw, proficiency skill, etc..), and can take damage up to 60% of the warlord's hit points before disappearing.
It also disappears if revealed by True Sight or removed by Dispel Magic.
The warlord has no reflection while the image is active, so he cannot create more than one Mirror Double.~
@7861 = ~You already control a mirror double. Wait for it to disappear before creating another.~
@7862 = ~Mirror Double (Illusion)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows the warlord to create a mirror double that can imitate his actions. More powerful than the 6th-level Physical Image spell, Mirror Double is created from the reflection of the caster and thus is no longer directly linked to him. So it can move independently of the caster and engage in combat. It cannot perform other actions such as opening a door or holding a conversation. Its illusory nature does not allow it to fully interact with the physical world.
When fighting, it can affect all creatures who believe it is real (and therefore cannot affect a creature immune to illusions). In this case, it fights with 60% of the warlord's abilities (THAC0, saving throw, proficiency skill, etc..), and can take damage up to 60% of the warlord's hit points before disappearing.
It also disappears if revealed by True Sight or removed by Dispel Magic.
The warlord has no reflection while the image is active, so he cannot create more than one Mirror Double.~
@7863 = ~Mirror Double (Illusion)
Level: 8
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows the warlord to create a mirror double of the recipient that can imitate his actions. More powerful than the 6th-level Physical Image spell, Mirror Double is created from the reflection of the recipient and thus is no longer directly linked to him. So it can move independently of the recipient and engage in combat. It cannot perform other actions such as opening a door or holding a conversation. Its illusory nature does not allow it to fully interact with the physical world.
When fighting, it can affect all creatures who believe it is real (and therefore cannot affect a creature immune to illusions). In this case, it fights with 60% of the warlord's abilities (THAC0, saving throw, proficiency skill, etc..), and can take damage up to 60% of the warlord's hit points before disappearing.
It also disappears if revealed by True Sight or removed by Dispel Magic.
The recipient has no reflection while the image is active and therefore cannot have more than one Mirror Double.~
@78631 = ~Mirror Double (Illusion)
Level: 8
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell allows the warlord to create a mirror double of the recipient that can imitate his actions. More powerful than the 6th-level Physical Image spell, Mirror Double is created from the reflection of the recipient and thus is no longer directly linked to him. So it can move independently of the recipient and engage in combat. It cannot perform other actions such as opening a door or holding a conversation. Its illusory nature does not allow it to fully interact with the physical world.
When fighting, it can affect all creatures who believe it is real (and therefore cannot affect a creature immune to illusions). In this case, it fights with 60% of the warlord's abilities (THAC0, saving throw, proficiency skill, etc..), and can take damage up to 60% of the warlord's hit points before disappearing.
It also disappears if revealed by True Sight or removed by Dispel Magic.
The recipient has no reflection while the image is active and therefore cannot have more than one Mirror Double.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
their image will last 13 rounds only.~

@787 = ~Stonebody~
@788 = ~Stonebody (Alteration)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

When the spell is cast, the body of the warlord turns into living stone, adopting the structure of the ground beneath him. This transformation grants him several distinct powers. As long as the spell lasts, he can only be wounded by weapons of +3 enchantment or higher, slashing and piercing weapons deal only one quarter of their normal damage. His natural armor class becomes 1 +/-1, depending on the type of stone and his strength increases by 3 points.
Spells that affect breathing or physiology such as clouds, poison, mold, cannot affect him. He ignores electricity attacks and suffers only 50% of fire and cold attacks.
Unfortunately, his movement becomes slow and cumbersome, which turns into a -2 penalty to movement speed and dexterity, -1 to his speed factor and THAC0.
The mage under stone shape also suffers a +1 increase to casting times and a 10% chance of spell failure, due to his voice that has become slow and guttural.
The mage must be touching the ground when casting the spell otherwise it will not work.~
@7881 = ~Stonebody (Alteration)
Level: 8
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

